{%- comment -%}
  Section: Wishlist product card (utility)
  Phase 5, Stage 3. Not a page-visible section — exists solely so
  assets/wishlist.js can fetch one real, Liquid-rendered product card for
  an arbitrary saved handle via Shopify's classic Section Rendering API:
    /products/<handle>?section_id=wishlist-product-card

  A section must be listed in the requesting template's `order` array to
  be section_id-fetchable at all (verified empirically before this stage
  was implemented — a section present only in `sections` and absent from
  `order` 404s). That means this renders on every real PDP load too; it's
  kept fully invisible there via the scoped [data-wishlist-product-card-
  source] rule in assets/theme.css (display:none on the wrapper, which
  removes it and everything inside from both layout and the accessibility
  tree/tab order — not just visually hidden).

  Renders the exact same snippets/product-card.liquid used on every
  collection grid, the homepage, and recommendations — image, price,
  badges, sizes, and the Stage 2 wishlist button — so nothing about a
  wishlist-page card is ever hand-built in JavaScript.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div data-wishlist-product-card-source>
  {%- render 'product-card', product: product -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Wishlist card",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
